  **Here is a proposed starting point for your implementation:**
  **Title:** Use Scheduled Pipeline
  **Summary:** A scheduled GitHub Actions workflow runs every Monday, calls the order service stock query with a read-only token, and emails the warehouse lead the items at or below their reorder point. It is not running yet.
  **Realizations:**
  - **Scheduler:** GitHub Actions scheduled workflow, which starts the check each week.
  - **Stock reader:** Order service stock query, called with a read-only token, which reads stock levels and reorder points without writing them.
  - **Alert sender:** Email to the warehouse lead, sending one alert that lists the items to restock.
  **Deployment:** A scheduled GitHub Actions workflow on a hosted runner, set to run on Mondays.
  **Data:** Stock levels and reorder points are read from the order service and not stored.
  **Security:** The stock query uses a read-only token held in repository secrets, so the job cannot write stock. No payment data is read (Protect Customer Payment Data).
  **Operations:** The job depends on the order service meeting Order Service Monthly Availability. This realization sets no separate operating target.
  **Deployed by:** GitHub Actions.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions to get Use Scheduled Pipeline up and running.
  **Managed by:** GitHub Actions.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will use GitHub Actions for managing Use Scheduled Pipeline once its running.
  **Language:** None.
  **Why it matters:** highway-codify will treat this as a Platform to manage as opposed to a coding project to write.
